WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.907
A useful finding identifies the
requirement, the specific design evidence

2
00:00:05.027 --> 00:00:06.315
and the gap.

3
00:00:06.435 --> 00:00:11.064
For example: drawing revision B contains a
cleaning pocket that has no

4
00:00:11.184 --> 00:00:14.022
reviewed rationale against the cleaning
concept.

5
00:00:14.142 --> 00:00:17.982
Assign an owner and define what evidence
would support closure.

6
00:00:18.102 --> 00:00:22.774
Avoid replacing the finding with a vague
status such as vendor to confirm.

7
00:00:22.894 --> 00:00:26.734
A due date helps manage work, but it does
not establish that the

8
00:00:26.854 --> 00:00:28.283
design is suitable.

9
00:00:28.903 --> 00:00:33.788
Our teaching review uses three distinct
outcomes: design evidence adequate,

10
00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:37.876
an open design finding, or a proposed
requirement change.

11
00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:42.263
These are course labels, not mandatory
regulatory terminology.

12
00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:46.906
If the vendor cannot meet a requirement,
assess options with the appropriate

13
00:00:47.026 --> 00:00:49.223
process and quality expertise.

14
00:00:49.343 --> 00:00:53.887
Do not close the gap by deleting the
requirement without impact review.

15
00:00:54.007 --> 00:00:58.508
A proposed change remains a proposal until
the applicable approval

16
00:00:58.628 --> 00:01:00.164
process accepts it.

17
00:01:00.784 --> 00:01:05.520
Conditional progression concerns a
particular next qualification activity,

18
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.582
not unrestricted production.

19
00:01:07.702 --> 00:01:12.096
In the fictional case, a missing product-
contact gasket basis prevents a

20
00:01:12.216 --> 00:01:14.051
final materials conclusion.

21
00:01:14.171 --> 00:01:17.712
An unrelated drawing review might
continue, but that does

22
00:01:17.832 --> 00:01:19.859
not authorize manufacturing.

23
00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:24.758
The responsible personnel need a
documented impact assessment and an

24
00:01:24.878 --> 00:01:27.608
authorized decision for the proposed
stage.

25
00:01:27.728 --> 00:01:31.780
Do not assume that the training author,
supplier or learner can grant

26
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.201
a site’s approval.

27
00:01:33.821 --> 00:01:38.664
When a gasket specification changes,
retain the earlier baseline and record

28
00:01:38.784 --> 00:01:40.704
why the new design was selected.

29
00:01:40.824 --> 00:01:45.027
Revisit contact compatibility, cleaning
assumptions and verification

30
00:01:45.147 --> 00:01:46.661
plans as appropriate.

31
00:01:46.781 --> 00:01:50.173
Update affected conclusions through the
quality system.

32
00:01:50.293 --> 00:01:54.757
The record should allow another reviewer
to reconstruct the decision without

33
00:01:54.877 --> 00:01:56.242
relying on memory.

34
00:01:56.362 --> 00:02:00.906
Your activity is to write an action
closure that references the revised

35
00:02:01.026 --> 00:02:04.205
evidence and preserves any outstanding
later tests.
